A||N||5||FieroSTETZ||how to make tribes 2 run properly (for all you who returned it)||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||04-16-2001||05:30 PM||||had the same symptoms you all listed on a pII 400 (my play around machine) but not on my 1.5, but figured it had to be more than just the cpu speed - turns out that the opengl drivers for tribes 2/3dfx aren't quite done yet, and it ran the game just fine after switching to direct3d, @ 40fps w/ pci voodoo3 (compared to 112 fps on the 1.5) but it WAS playable - anyone who has it, try the direct3d||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-16-2001||07:40 PM||||As some may know. 3DFX is no more. Bought out by N'vidia. there are several news groups covering them and one site in europe that is keeping the end of life 3Dfx products supported. <P>Official support from N'vidia appears limited to the remnant of the 3Dfx web site. I.E. some driver downloads and that's it.<P>Any games out in the last 9 months to a year are likely affected by this.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cameron||04-16-2001||11:50 PM||||3DFX has been no more for awhile now ... even before they were bought out they stopped making video cards after the last set relieced, the voodoo 4 and 5's.  I could see that it was going to happen since Guillemot and Hercules joined.  Their 3D Prophet is a really good card.  Yes, there are some better ones not to start the contraversy, but still ... But I agree for those who have 3DFX cards it is too bad.  It always sucks to see a good video card company go.<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||04-17-2001||01:26 AM||||I had it set for Direct3D, but it still ran like faeces. It simply won't run fast on a Celeron.||||reg||1
